    "forensics": "The losing cluster exposes three primary vulnerabilities: premature breakeven stop triggers on ICICIBANK (#2) and AXISBANK (#6) that yielded positive gross P&L but net losses due to transaction fee drag (\u20b944.12 total fees across 12 trades), and mid-morning liquidity fade whipsaws on INFY (#1, #12) and TATASTEEL (#3) between 10:25 and 10:40 IST where exact 0.70% stops were hunted. Furthermore, late-session entries like ICICIBANK (#9 at 14:10 IST) suffered from decaying intraday follow-through, resulting in an EOD square-off loss amplified by brokerage and statutory charges.",
    "learning": "In small-capital NSE cash equity accounts, high statutory and brokerage fee ratios require wider breakeven trigger thresholds (above 1.0R) to prevent turning winning directional setups into net fee-drag losses during routine intraday mean-reversion pullbacks, alongside higher volume conviction to filter out mid-morning fakeouts.",
