    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #30 Quantitative Review & Parameter Mutation\nPhase 2 Out-of-Sample testing with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash achieved a 50.0% win rate and a 0.95 Profit Factor (\u20b9-4.60 Net P&L), demonstrating strong gross alpha that was narrowly negated by \u20b944.12 in transaction costs. Forensic analysis of the losing trade cluster revealed that two of the six losses (`ICICIBANK` #2 and `AXISBANK` #6) were actually gross-profitable trades choked prematurely by the `0.85R` breakeven trigger during normal mid-day consolidations, converting potential runners into net fee-drag losses. Meanwhile, full stop-outs in `INFY` and `TATASTEEL` occurred during the 10:25\u201310:40 IST post-opening exhaustion window. To push the desk into net profitability for Cycle #31, we are expanding `breakeven_trigger_r` to `1.15` to give winning trades room to breathe and clear the fee hurdle, increasing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to `2.55` to demand stronger institutional participation against mid-morning fakeouts, slightly tightening `min_sl_pct` to `0.65%` to cap downside tail risk on failed sweeps, and raising `min_target_pct` to `1.45%` to maximize reward-to-fee asymmetry."
